{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.FrobeniusPairing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.FrobeniusPairing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.hasNonDegeneratePairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.hasNonDegeneratePairing","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing.lean#L83-L95","doc":"A Frobenius–Hopf datum with snake identities already has a\nnon-degenerate canonical pairing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusPairing.NonDegenerate.snake_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusPairing.NonDegenerate.snake_right","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing.lean#L78-L78","doc":"Snake identity (right): the mirror composite equals `𝟙_A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusPairing.NonDegenerate.snake_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusPairing.NonDegenerate.snake_left","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Snake identity (left): the composite\n`A →[ρ⁻¹] A ⊗ 𝟙 →[id ⊗ η̃] A ⊗ A ⊗ A →[α⁻¹] (A ⊗ A) ⊗ A\n →[⟨-,-⟩_F ⊗ id] 𝟙 ⊗ A →[λ] A`\nequals `𝟙_A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusPairing.NonDegenerate.coevaluation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusPairing.NonDegenerate.coevaluation","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The coevaluation morphism `η̃ : 𝟙 → A ⊗ A` dual to the pairing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusPairing.NonDegenerate.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusPairing.NonDegenerate.mk","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusPairing.NonDegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusPairing.NonDegenerate","kind":"structure","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing.lean#L61-L81","doc":"Non-degeneracy of the Frobenius pairing: the induced map\n`A → A∨` (currying one argument of the pairing) is an isomorphism.\nStated as: the snake identities hold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusPairing.symmetric_of_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusPairing.symmetric_of_comm","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing.lean#L49-L59","doc":"The Frobenius pairing is symmetric when the multiplication is\ncommutative (i.e., `μ ∘ β = μ` where `β` is the braiding).\nIn this case `⟨a, b⟩_F = ⟨b, a⟩_F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.canonicalPairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.canonicalPairing","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing.lean#L41-L47","doc":"Construct the canonical Frobenius pairing from a Frobenius–Hopf datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusPairing.pairing_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusPairing.pairing_eq","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing.lean#L39-L39","doc":"The pairing factors through multiplication then the Frobenius form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusPairing.pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusPairing.pairing","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing.lean#L37-L37","doc":"The Frobenius pairing morphism `⟨-,-⟩_F : A ⊗ A → 𝟙`,\ndefined as the composite `λ ∘ μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusPairing.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusPairing.mk","kind":"ctor","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusPairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusPairing","kind":"structure","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing.lean#L21-L39","doc":"**Frobenius pairing**: the composite `λ ∘ μ : A ⊗ A → 𝟙`.\n\nGiven a Frobenius–Hopf object `(A, μ, λ)` in a monoidal category `C`,\nthe Frobenius pairing is `⟨a, b⟩_F = λ(μ(a ⊗ b))`, i.e. the composite\n`A ⊗ A →[μ] A →[λ] 𝟙`.\n\nNon-degeneracy means this pairing induces an isomorphism `A ≅ A∨`.\nEquivalently, the snake identities hold with respect to a coevaluation\n`η̃ : 𝟙 → A ⊗ A`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:frobenius-pairing}`\nRef: [kock2004] https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511615443 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:frobenius-pairing","label":"def:frobenius-pairing","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}